# Candidate summary — S013505

Adds `src/include/linux/bcma/bcma_regs.rs` with immutable provenance for the
pinned BCMA register header. The candidate maps all 74 object-like C macros to
public Rust constants, preserving their names, literal values, C integer
literal signedness (`i32` or `u32`), aliases, and the lone arithmetic
expression (`64 * 1024 * 1024`). It has no executable logic or replacement
mechanism.
